<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!-- Liveness probe for every declared research browser profile.
     See browser_session_health.py.

     WHY 30 MINUTES AND NOT FASTER. The probe opens a REAL Chrome and loads a
     page on the very surface it is trying to stay signed into. A five-minute
     probe is itself the bot-like access pattern that gets a session flagged, so
     a faster check would break the thing it checks. Worst-case notification lag
     is half an hour, against a repair that is a human sign-in happening at most
     once a day.

     WHY NOT /usr/bin/python3. Every other com.kipi.* plist here runs the system
     python, which is right for a job that reads JSON. This one drives
     Playwright, and measured 2026-08-30 on this Mac:
         /usr/bin/python3           ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'playwright'
         /opt/homebrew/bin/python3  3.14.6, playwright imports
     Copying the system-python line would ship a job launchd loads happily and
     that dies on import forever, visible only in a log nobody reads.
     test_plist_uses_an_interpreter_that_actually_has_playwright pins this.

     WHY StartInterval AND NOT StartCalendarInterval. A calendar job is skipped
     outright when the Mac is off at fire time; launchd does not catch up on
     wake. This must resume on its own after a reboot or a closed lid.

     The window is thrown far off-screen by browser_session.py rather than run
     headless: headless returns 403 on the surfaces this exists for (NodeSeek,
     measured 2026-08-27), and 96 visible windows a day is how a job gets killed.

     Install: bash q-system/.q-system/scripts/install-plist.sh com.kipi.browser-session-health
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.kipi.browser-session-health</string>
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>HOME</key><string>__HOME__</string>
    <key>USER</key><string>__USER__</string>
    <key>LOGNAME</key><string>__USER__</string>
    <key>PATH</key><string>__HOME__/.local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
  </dict>
  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin/python3</string>
    <string>__KIPI_REPO__/q-system/.q-system/scripts/browser_session_health.py</string>
  </array>
  <key>StartInterval</key><integer>1800</integer>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><true/>
  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>__HOME__/.config/kipi/logs/browser-session-health.out.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>__HOME__/.config/kipi/logs/browser-session-health.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
